WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.190 --> 00:00:01.530
Do you want to hear a secret?

00:00:01.530 --> 00:00:02.940
Hold on.

00:00:02.940 --> 00:00:08.410
Before I quench your curiosity, let me remind
you that some things are better off left not

00:00:08.410 --> 00:00:09.469
knowing.

00:00:09.469 --> 00:00:14.949
Pry around long enough and you’re sure to
find something you weren’t looking for.

00:00:14.949 --> 00:00:20.930
That is to say, not every treasure chest is
filled with gold coins, elegant jewelry, and

00:00:20.930 --> 00:00:22.840
expensive relics.

00:00:22.840 --> 00:00:25.340
Maybe it’s not even a treasure chest at
all.

00:00:25.340 --> 00:00:28.930
Dumpsters do look quite similar, don’t they?

00:00:28.930 --> 00:00:32.820
Peek inside and you might find rotting meat,
an army of maggots, and a smell that stings

00:00:32.820 --> 00:00:33.820
your nostrils.

00:00:33.820 --> 00:00:38.079
So, do you want to hear a secret now?

00:00:38.079 --> 00:00:39.949
Pshh.

00:00:39.949 --> 00:00:41.019
Of course, you do.

00:00:41.019 --> 00:00:45.300
No disclaimer could stand in the way of humanity
and hot gossip.

00:00:45.300 --> 00:00:47.339
Look at the world around you.

00:00:47.339 --> 00:00:50.300
Everything revolves around information.

00:00:50.300 --> 00:00:53.399
The more we know, the more we can say.

00:00:53.399 --> 00:00:57.829
And is there anything people want more than
something to say?

00:00:57.829 --> 00:01:02.030
Next time you’re at a nice restaurant with
a group of friends or coworkers or family,

00:01:02.030 --> 00:01:07.030
look across from you and notice how hard lips
have to refrain from belting out, interjecting,

00:01:07.030 --> 00:01:09.250
or adding two cents.

00:01:09.250 --> 00:01:13.860
Humans can’t help but throw their words
into the universe, as if they will echo in

00:01:13.860 --> 00:01:16.580
importance for eternity.

00:01:16.580 --> 00:01:19.110
Some might say that listening is a skill.

00:01:19.110 --> 00:01:23.580
However, you can argue that it is simply a
prerequisite to speaking.

00:01:23.580 --> 00:01:25.180
It is a deal we make.

00:01:25.180 --> 00:01:26.730
A compromise.

00:01:26.730 --> 00:01:29.290
If we listen, then we get to speak!

00:01:29.290 --> 00:01:32.250
If we hear a secret, we get to share it.

00:01:32.250 --> 00:01:38.180
So we spend our lives listening, observing,
and gathering information about the people,

00:01:38.180 --> 00:01:40.550
places, and things around us.

00:01:40.550 --> 00:01:45.140
Philosophers and scientists like to call it,
“The pursuit of truth.”

00:01:45.140 --> 00:01:46.140
But who are we kidding?

00:01:46.140 --> 00:01:47.740
It is a chore.

00:01:47.740 --> 00:01:53.340
A task completed only for the prize that comes
with it: the chance to speak about what we’ve

00:01:53.340 --> 00:01:55.750
seen, heard, and learned.

00:01:55.750 --> 00:02:01.530
Most often, this journey of gathering information
isn’t as profound as we pretend it is.

00:02:01.530 --> 00:02:05.190
Digging around other people’s business is
no noble task.

00:02:05.190 --> 00:02:10.319
But curiosity is like a shiny shovel, and
to let a tool like this rust in the shed would

00:02:10.319 --> 00:02:11.319
be a sin.

00:02:11.319 --> 00:02:12.319
Wouldn’t it?

00:02:12.319 --> 00:02:16.450
So, with that said, let’s stop pretending
we don’t love TMZ.

00:02:16.450 --> 00:02:19.690
Let’s indulge in our lust for secrets.

00:02:19.690 --> 00:02:21.220
Let’s get digging.

00:02:21.220 --> 00:02:25.970
Deep into the mystery of SCP-1903.

00:02:25.970 --> 00:02:31.050
Like with understanding any artifact, culture,
or ideology, we have to first look at the

00:02:31.050 --> 00:02:34.950
earliest origins of our subject to comprehend
its current state.

00:02:34.950 --> 00:02:41.030
This is to say, SCP-1903 wasn’t always SCP-1903.

00:02:41.030 --> 00:02:43.061
Once upon a time, she was Jackie.

00:02:43.061 --> 00:02:44.190
Jackie Barter.

00:02:44.190 --> 00:02:50.610
A woman who dedicated herself to her job,
trying to make a better life for herself.

00:02:50.610 --> 00:02:53.810
Jackie Barter valued her work above anything
else.

00:02:53.810 --> 00:02:56.220
She did her job and never complained.

00:02:56.220 --> 00:02:58.330
She showed up early and always smiled.

00:02:58.330 --> 00:03:02.300
Whether she enjoyed it, however, was another
thing.

00:03:02.300 --> 00:03:05.790
It’s hard to know anyone’s true feelings
at their workplace.

00:03:05.790 --> 00:03:08.790
But we can speculate that her clients enjoyed
it more.

00:03:08.790 --> 00:03:11.890
So, what was it that she did exactly for work?

00:03:11.890 --> 00:03:14.690
What was her job title when she filed taxes?

00:03:14.690 --> 00:03:17.590
What did her day-to-day shift look like?

00:03:17.590 --> 00:03:19.849
If only it was that easy.

00:03:19.849 --> 00:03:25.459
She handled her responsibilities behind closed
doors, and there was an agreement between

00:03:25.459 --> 00:03:31.260
her, her clients, and her boss – Mr. Donnar
– not to speak of what happened behind said

00:03:31.260 --> 00:03:32.349
doors.

00:03:32.349 --> 00:03:35.660
In a way, these customers were paying for
privacy.

00:03:35.660 --> 00:03:40.800
At the same time, and maybe more importantly,
they were paying for Jackie.

00:03:40.800 --> 00:03:44.780
Jackie Barter was one of the primary reasons
why Mr. Donnar was a success.

00:03:44.780 --> 00:03:47.770
Sure, he had a knack for business.

00:03:47.770 --> 00:03:50.920
He knew how to operate in the shadows of anonymity.

00:03:50.920 --> 00:03:52.890
He knew how to turn a profit.

00:03:52.890 --> 00:03:56.640
But most importantly, he knew what his clients
wanted.

00:03:56.640 --> 00:03:58.819
And what they wanted was Jackie.

00:03:58.819 --> 00:04:01.060
But what exactly did she do?

00:04:01.060 --> 00:04:03.150
What was she offering?

00:04:03.150 --> 00:04:04.550
Why did they want her?

00:04:04.550 --> 00:04:08.349
The tight-lipped Donnar never made those easy
questions to answer.

00:04:08.349 --> 00:04:14.670
However, what we do know is that she was in
the service industry… and she wasn’t bringing

00:04:14.670 --> 00:04:17.389
food or drinks to her clients.

00:04:17.389 --> 00:04:20.660
Jackie Barter, herself, was enough for them.

00:04:20.660 --> 00:04:27.080
She brought her energy, her smile, her personality,
her charm, and her glow.

00:04:27.080 --> 00:04:30.780
She dressed in a white dress and wore novelty
bunny ears.

00:04:30.780 --> 00:04:32.400
The wardrobe never changed.

00:04:32.400 --> 00:04:33.950
It never had to.

00:04:33.950 --> 00:04:38.100
While customers came to Donnar’s establishment
to mix things up from their normal lives,

00:04:38.100 --> 00:04:41.830
when they were there, they didn’t want change.

00:04:41.830 --> 00:04:44.230
They wanted the same thing each time.

00:04:44.230 --> 00:04:49.150
They knew what they wanted, and it was Jackie
Barter.

00:04:49.150 --> 00:04:52.770
Jackie Barter in a white dress and bunny ears.

00:04:52.770 --> 00:04:57.930
What she actually did, however, isn’t as
clear, but if you were to speculate, you’d

00:04:57.930 --> 00:05:01.010
likely come to some version of the truth.

00:05:01.010 --> 00:05:03.930
What is clear is who she did it for.

00:05:03.930 --> 00:05:09.100
A man who we will refer to as A.F was her
top client.

00:05:09.100 --> 00:05:12.250
A.F managed the chemical plant a few blocks
from the establishment.

00:05:12.250 --> 00:05:17.260
He had a wife, a high-income job, and had
the means to live a good life.

00:05:17.260 --> 00:05:21.370
He had things going for him, everything he
could ever want.

00:05:21.370 --> 00:05:25.500
But like any man built of vices, he wanted
more.

00:05:25.500 --> 00:05:29.340
Mr. Donnar’s establishment was made for
people like AF.

00:05:29.340 --> 00:05:33.750
It was a place where people could be influenced
by the devil on their left shoulder and not

00:05:33.750 --> 00:05:35.130
be judged for it.

00:05:35.130 --> 00:05:38.890
It was a place for depravity detached from
morality.

00:05:38.890 --> 00:05:42.949
It was a place where you didn’t have to
shape your behavior to the expectations of

00:05:42.949 --> 00:05:46.180
society, family, or friends.

00:05:46.180 --> 00:05:51.060
More than that, it was a place where people
themselves didn’t feel guilty for what they

00:05:51.060 --> 00:05:52.060
did.

00:05:52.060 --> 00:05:57.530
Mr. Donnar created a place where people could
act on their impulses, enjoy themselves, walk

00:05:57.530 --> 00:06:01.720
out, go home, and leave their shame at the
door.

00:06:01.720 --> 00:06:04.230
AF loved every aspect of it.

00:06:04.230 --> 00:06:06.150
And so, he became a local.

00:06:06.150 --> 00:06:09.710
He went frequently, and he always requested
Jackie.

00:06:09.710 --> 00:06:13.550
Donnar operated his business in a vague, mysterious
building.

00:06:13.550 --> 00:06:17.590
The type of place you’d have to Yelp three
times before entering just to make sure you’re

00:06:17.590 --> 00:06:18.639
at the right address.

00:06:18.639 --> 00:06:23.680
It looked abandoned, and yet, you could feel
the life behind those doors.

00:06:23.680 --> 00:06:25.030
It pulled you in.

00:06:25.030 --> 00:06:28.790
Inside, there were rooms lined up like a hotel
hallway.

00:06:28.790 --> 00:06:35.669
Behind one of those particular doors waited
not just one man, but rather a crew of friends.

00:06:35.669 --> 00:06:38.320
AF always brought about three or four people
with him.

00:06:38.320 --> 00:06:41.050
Why he brought them isn’t understood.

00:06:41.050 --> 00:06:44.040
Did he feel safer in his sins when shared
with others?

00:06:44.040 --> 00:06:47.449
Or is it that he was trying to impress them?

00:06:47.449 --> 00:06:51.430
Or maybe he was up to no good and wanted to
have the numbers on his side.

00:06:51.430 --> 00:06:56.830
What we do know, is that whoever these men
were, AF had an abundance of them.

00:06:56.830 --> 00:07:01.789
Each time he visited the establishment, he
brought a different group of people with him.

00:07:01.789 --> 00:07:03.880
But the variance ended there.

00:07:03.880 --> 00:07:09.650
Because each time, his request was exactly
the same: the “woman dressed in white".

00:07:09.650 --> 00:07:12.600
He wanted Jackie, and only Jackie.

00:07:12.600 --> 00:07:14.740
She was his preferred handler.

00:07:14.740 --> 00:07:16.770
The reasons for this aren’t clear.

00:07:16.770 --> 00:07:19.690
It might be as simple as a man having a specific
taste.

00:07:19.690 --> 00:07:22.210
They might have gotten along quite well.

00:07:22.210 --> 00:07:24.850
Or maybe there’s more to it.

00:07:24.850 --> 00:07:26.580
Maybe he was up to something.

00:07:26.580 --> 00:07:29.300
Why he chose her, we don’t know.

00:07:29.300 --> 00:07:32.020
But we do know he loved his time with Jackie.

00:07:32.020 --> 00:07:35.060
Little did he know, his time with her was
running out.

00:07:35.060 --> 00:07:41.210
Soon she would be someone, or something, entirely
new.

00:07:41.210 --> 00:07:43.190
SCP-1903.

00:07:43.190 --> 00:07:46.960
What happened that night behind closed doors,
we aren’t sure.

00:07:46.960 --> 00:07:49.860
But don’t let that stop you from speculating.

00:07:49.860 --> 00:07:54.631
After AF returned home, his wife went to Donnar’s
establishment looking for information, no

00:07:54.631 --> 00:07:59.540
different than you are seeking information
right now, listening closely, waiting for

00:07:59.540 --> 00:08:01.390
the next bomb to drop.

00:08:01.390 --> 00:08:03.750
Only she wasn’t at her computer.

00:08:03.750 --> 00:08:06.210
She was actively fighting for it.

00:08:06.210 --> 00:08:10.930
Donnar, being a man dedicated to privacy,
kept his mouth shut and sent her away.

00:08:10.930 --> 00:08:12.979
But AF’s wife didn’t give up.

00:08:12.979 --> 00:08:15.140
She knew something was off.

00:08:15.140 --> 00:08:17.819
And so she tracked Jackie down after hours.

00:08:17.819 --> 00:08:22.350
Unlike her confrontational encounter with
Donnar, she was able to ease into a friendly

00:08:22.350 --> 00:08:28.270
conversation with Jackie and coax information
out of her, slowly but surely.

00:08:28.270 --> 00:08:31.460
Jackie opened up and told her everything.

00:08:31.460 --> 00:08:35.719
She told her all about AF’s late nights
spent there at Donnar’s establishment and

00:08:35.719 --> 00:08:38.099
about the men he’d bring with him.

00:08:38.099 --> 00:08:42.750
More specifically, Jackie explained to her
what happened the night in question.

00:08:42.750 --> 00:08:47.250
And whatever it was, it was enough for Jackie
not to come in the next day.

00:08:47.250 --> 00:08:51.510
And in the days following, that’s when everything
changed for Jackie.

00:08:51.510 --> 00:08:56.190
Over the course of the next few days, she
painfully morphed into what we see her to

00:08:56.190 --> 00:08:59.000
be now.

00:08:59.000 --> 00:09:00.000
SCP-1903.

00:09:00.000 --> 00:09:02.070
It started in her face.

00:09:02.070 --> 00:09:04.510
Nothing that would concern anyone at first
glance.

00:09:04.510 --> 00:09:07.070
Her cheeks turned slightly pink.

00:09:07.070 --> 00:09:09.750
But the symptoms wouldn’t be overlooked
for long.

00:09:09.750 --> 00:09:12.029
She developed dark claw-like hands and feet.

00:09:12.029 --> 00:09:16.570
The skin on her face turned into what looks
like a paper mâché-styled rabbit mask.

00:09:16.570 --> 00:09:21.720
Her bunny ears no longer were just for show,
but rather they are entirely responsible for

00:09:21.720 --> 00:09:23.700
her ability to hear.

00:09:23.700 --> 00:09:27.930
She began to produce mercury and blood through
the pores of her hands and feet.

00:09:27.930 --> 00:09:30.750
No longer was she Jackie Barter.

00:09:30.750 --> 00:09:35.490
The Foundation stepped in and took her into
their own custody and deemed her SCP-1903.

00:09:35.490 --> 00:09:40.430
This, however, did not come without consequence
for the Foundation.

00:09:40.430 --> 00:09:45.700
The discovery of SCP-1903 and the knowledge
obtained and passed along should not have

00:09:45.700 --> 00:09:46.700
been celebrated.

00:09:46.700 --> 00:09:50.680
But they didn’t know this until the party
had already started.

00:09:50.680 --> 00:09:54.770
And when the balloons began to pop, it was
already too late.

00:09:54.770 --> 00:09:59.540
Let this be a lesson, be careful of the secrets
you tell.

00:09:59.540 --> 00:10:04.420
Unlike most curiosities, this one came at
a cost no contestant on The Price is Right

00:10:04.420 --> 00:10:06.190
could ever have guessed.

00:10:06.190 --> 00:10:11.390
We are creatures who crave information, and
we will dig around until we get it.

00:10:11.390 --> 00:10:16.360
And once retrieved, it is instinct to hold
it up and show the world.

00:10:16.360 --> 00:10:18.200
Mostly, this is innocuous.

00:10:18.200 --> 00:10:23.760
However, sometimes, when someone spills the
tea… we all get burned.

00:10:23.760 --> 00:10:27.779
And that is exactly what happened.

00:10:27.779 --> 00:10:32.580
SCP-1903 was discovered by the Foundation
to harbor a slow-acting infohazard.

00:10:32.580 --> 00:10:37.130
The effects of this infohazard are triggered
when the subject learns three important details

00:10:37.130 --> 00:10:38.420
of Jackie's story.

00:10:38.420 --> 00:10:40.980
1) AF’s full name

00:10:40.980 --> 00:10:43.541
2) AF’s actions toward Jackie

00:10:43.541 --> 00:10:47.620
3) And Jackie’s response to AF’s actions.

00:10:47.620 --> 00:10:53.550
Sorry, Lebron, Bosh, and Wade, but no big
three in NBA history has ever been as powerful

00:10:53.550 --> 00:10:54.769
as this one.

00:10:54.769 --> 00:10:57.830
It is the catalyst for years of damage.

00:10:57.830 --> 00:11:03.330
If not guarded properly, it has the force
to dismantle entire dynasties.

00:11:03.330 --> 00:11:07.520
As the Foundation spread this information
throughout personal, so spread the infection

00:11:07.520 --> 00:11:09.680
across the research team.

00:11:09.680 --> 00:11:13.029
Anyone who learned too much of the story was
and will be afflicted.

00:11:13.029 --> 00:11:15.170
But what exactly does that look like?

00:11:15.170 --> 00:11:19.560
Well, subjects will begin showing symptoms
of mercury poisoning, and large parts of skin

00:11:19.560 --> 00:11:24.910
will flake off exclusively around the facial
area two days after exposure to the trigger

00:11:24.910 --> 00:11:25.959
information.

00:11:25.959 --> 00:11:31.310
After five days, typically when the pigmentation
of the affected area is a pure white in color,

00:11:31.310 --> 00:11:36.790
the dermis will begin to form a protective
layer of similar composition to SCP-1903's

00:11:36.790 --> 00:11:41.050
mask, with the exclusion of any traces of
mercury.

00:11:41.050 --> 00:11:45.890
This layer will continue to form until it
covers the entire facial area and will eventually

00:11:45.890 --> 00:11:52.709
appear to resemble a paper mâché animal
mask of a similar fashion to SCP-1903's, which

00:11:52.709 --> 00:11:57.880
typically resembles rabbits, cats, wolves,
foxes, and rats.

00:11:57.880 --> 00:12:02.580
They will go biologically deaf, and they will
only be able to hear if they continue to wear

00:12:02.580 --> 00:12:04.070
these ears.

00:12:04.070 --> 00:12:09.850
Over the course of this change, the hands
and feet will undergo a pigmentation shift,

00:12:09.850 --> 00:12:11.520
darkening considerably.

00:12:11.520 --> 00:12:16.380
Their nails will sharpen, growing into claws
over time, and the subject's hearing will

00:12:16.380 --> 00:12:21.649
transfer to the nearest set of novelty ears
which represent the animal that their masks

00:12:21.649 --> 00:12:22.649
resemble.

00:12:22.649 --> 00:12:26.800
Once subjects have found these ears, they
will show reluctance to take them off.

00:12:26.800 --> 00:12:30.661
It is unclear if this is because they have
built a bond with their identity, or if it

00:12:30.661 --> 00:12:33.960
is simply the case of them trying to preserve
their hearing.

00:12:33.960 --> 00:12:38.490
Furthermore, if a pair of ears become damaged
to the point where repair without spare parts

00:12:38.490 --> 00:12:42.560
is impossible, the subject will become permanently
deaf.

00:12:42.560 --> 00:12:47.019
And they will be left wishing their deafness
had come sooner, saving them from hearing

00:12:47.019 --> 00:12:51.330
Jackie’s secret, saving them from the curse
that comes with it.

00:12:51.330 --> 00:12:53.770
Maybe they even wish they mute too.

00:12:53.770 --> 00:12:58.329
Because once an affected subject tells a non-affected
subject about the trigger information, the

00:12:58.329 --> 00:13:03.370
normal subject will undergo the changes the
affected subject went through up until that

00:13:03.370 --> 00:13:04.370
point.

00:13:04.370 --> 00:13:06.850
Thus continuing this chain of unfortunate
fate.

00:13:06.850 --> 00:13:11.380
Two to three days later, blood will begin
to seep through the pores in the subject's

00:13:11.380 --> 00:13:13.390
hands, feet, and gums.

00:13:13.390 --> 00:13:18.440
Within a few hours, mercury will begin to
appear in the subject's bloodstream.

00:13:18.440 --> 00:13:22.530
This does not physically affect the subject
or other subjects in a similar state.

00:13:22.530 --> 00:13:26.089
However, it does severely affect the subject's
mental health.

00:13:26.089 --> 00:13:30.579
Many afflicted subjects have been reported
to go to extreme measures to remove the mask

00:13:30.579 --> 00:13:32.670
that has overtaken their face.

00:13:32.670 --> 00:13:34.490
AF was one of them.

00:13:34.490 --> 00:13:40.089
He sawed at it with a knife until his face
was, well, faceless.

00:13:40.089 --> 00:13:44.600
This means of infection by way of info hazard
was most notably observed with researcher

00:13:44.600 --> 00:13:49.880
Hayward, when he was reading revision 2 of
SCP-1903.

00:13:49.880 --> 00:13:56.089
By the time he finished, he saw SCP-1903 staring
at him from across the cell through the observatory

00:13:56.089 --> 00:13:57.089
window.

00:13:57.089 --> 00:13:59.740
She was trying to warn him not to read it.

00:13:59.740 --> 00:14:02.820
She didn't say anything, but she shushed him.

00:14:02.820 --> 00:14:06.660
He pressed the button for a photograph and
tried to talk to her through the intercom,

00:14:06.660 --> 00:14:10.210
but when he did, she just sat back down on
her cot.

00:14:10.210 --> 00:14:14.260
He assumed that she realized he was reading
her file and then tried to warn him not to

00:14:14.260 --> 00:14:15.260
tell anyone.

00:14:15.260 --> 00:14:20.660
While the story of SCP-1903 was going around
infecting people and causing them intense

00:14:20.660 --> 00:14:27.430
physical and psychological pain, SCP-1903
herself was trying to save them from it.

00:14:27.430 --> 00:14:30.709
This is the tragic through-line of the story.

00:14:30.709 --> 00:14:34.570
Jackie Barter spent her whole life making
other people feel better.

00:14:34.570 --> 00:14:39.730
In most cases, this meant sacrificing her
time and energy to do so.

00:14:39.730 --> 00:14:42.960
And her payment for these services wasn’t
fair.

00:14:42.960 --> 00:14:43.960
What did she get?

00:14:43.960 --> 00:14:46.670
She was sentenced to life under strict supervision.

00:14:46.670 --> 00:14:48.540
A life in pain.

00:14:48.540 --> 00:14:51.910
A life in a body that isn’t her own.

00:14:51.910 --> 00:14:54.050
But this is often overlooked.

00:14:54.050 --> 00:15:00.010
The most documented and studied pain wasn’t
of SCP-1903’s but rather the personnel who

00:15:00.010 --> 00:15:01.580
were affected by her story.

00:15:01.580 --> 00:15:07.779
In fact, there are few documented records
of how SCP-1903 itself feels.

00:15:07.779 --> 00:15:13.180
However, we have interviews with researcher
Hayward explaining how he felt after being

00:15:13.180 --> 00:15:14.180
affected.

00:15:14.180 --> 00:15:18.610
And maybe, with time, as Hayward moves further
and further away from his time as a normal

00:15:18.610 --> 00:15:23.050
human being, we will begin to disregard his
pain too.

00:15:23.050 --> 00:15:26.649
In science, empathy often finds a way to elude
us.

00:15:26.649 --> 00:15:31.320
With each new study, we move closer to an
objective understanding, but at the cost of

00:15:31.320 --> 00:15:34.589
traveling further and further from its emotional
makeup.

00:15:34.589 --> 00:15:38.339
Regarding Hayward, he initially felt fine
after the affliction.

00:15:38.339 --> 00:15:42.519
But in a couple of hours, the affected areas
started to feel irritated.

00:15:42.519 --> 00:15:44.209
Nothing that couldn’t be managed though.

00:15:44.209 --> 00:15:47.220
He didn’t think much of it until the second
day.

00:15:47.220 --> 00:15:51.449
By then, it felt like he had spent the day
on the beach staring up at the hot sun.

00:15:51.449 --> 00:15:55.329
But he remembers not having been in the sun
at all that day.

00:15:55.329 --> 00:16:00.680
Even under a layer of clouds and low temperatures,
the skin on his face felt to have been roasting

00:16:00.680 --> 00:16:02.160
as if in the oven.

00:16:02.160 --> 00:16:04.700
His face was slowly peeling off.

00:16:04.700 --> 00:16:08.180
If he tugged at the corner, he swore it would
have ripped off like a Band-Aid.

00:16:08.180 --> 00:16:10.779
The pain and discomfort didn’t end there.

00:16:10.779 --> 00:16:15.520
The testing for mercury wasn't much fun either
for him, however, he was quite reluctant to

00:16:15.520 --> 00:16:20.100
go into details about how the procedure was
done, similar to how your dad would respond

00:16:20.100 --> 00:16:21.899
if you asked him about his colonoscopy.

00:16:21.899 --> 00:16:25.730
Even now, Hayward’s face is still tender.

00:16:25.730 --> 00:16:28.970
A gentle kiss on the cheek would feel like
a pinch.

00:16:28.970 --> 00:16:30.880
But the worst pain wasn’t physical.

00:16:30.880 --> 00:16:34.190
It was the mental games it played with his
head.

00:16:34.190 --> 00:16:35.940
He experienced hallucinations.

00:16:35.940 --> 00:16:40.300
He started seeing them around the time he
noticed that the mask finished growing.

00:16:40.300 --> 00:16:44.570
They blended with reality and it took him
time to start recognizing their onset.

00:16:44.570 --> 00:16:51.100
He could tell he was hallucinating if he focused
on people's clothing, because in his hallucinations

00:16:51.100 --> 00:16:56.240
their outfits would change until everyone
was wearing a white tux or a white evening

00:16:56.240 --> 00:16:57.240
gown.

00:16:57.240 --> 00:17:00.130
The dresses would be classy yet revealing.

00:17:00.130 --> 00:17:03.490
Similar to how the women would dress at Donnar’s
establishment.

00:17:03.490 --> 00:17:08.360
In fact, most everything in the hallucinations
could be called back to Donnar’s.

00:17:08.360 --> 00:17:12.980
The people in the hallucinations would be
wearing masks of different animal types, just

00:17:12.980 --> 00:17:15.359
like Jackie and her coworkers.

00:17:15.359 --> 00:17:19.959
Hayward said it looked like a masquerade where
he was the center of attention.

00:17:19.959 --> 00:17:24.100
Everyone would turn their heads to face him,
even if their necks should've snapped.

00:17:24.100 --> 00:17:27.039
They’d turn a full 180.

00:17:27.039 --> 00:17:29.460
And they’d just glare.

00:17:29.460 --> 00:17:32.360
These hallucinations would last close to thirty
seconds.

00:17:32.360 --> 00:17:35.889
And during that half minute, one thing stood
out specifically.

00:17:35.889 --> 00:17:40.830
There would be a man leaning against the wall,
not wearing a mask.

00:17:40.830 --> 00:17:46.610
He was the only one who wasn’t in stylish
evening wear, so he kind of sticks out.

00:17:46.610 --> 00:17:51.389
He can’t be made out clearly, but by studying
the description, The Foundation believes it

00:17:51.389 --> 00:17:53.830
to be a vision of Donnar.

00:17:53.830 --> 00:17:57.629
Could Donnar be a more important piece to
this story than we give him credit?

00:17:57.629 --> 00:18:02.629
The person trying hardest to silence the story
must have the most skin in the game of secrets,

00:18:02.629 --> 00:18:03.629
right?

00:18:03.629 --> 00:18:07.979
Either way, we can all learn a lesson from
Donnar and keep quiet from time to time.

00:18:07.979 --> 00:18:09.889
I will say it again.

00:18:09.889 --> 00:18:14.359
Sometimes when someone spills the tea… we
all get burned.

00:18:14.359 --> 00:18:20.609
Now go check out “SCP-3887 - Monster Under
the Bed” and “The Horror of Body Stealing

00:18:20.609 --> 00:18:26.059
Rain - SCP-3300” for more haunting anomalies
that’ll stay with you forever…

